This product will include software developed by third parties under permissive
licences. Attributions are added to this file as the dependencies land:

- blocky (https://github.com/0xERR0R/blocky), Apache-2.0: matcher and list
  pipeline designs (string caches, suffix sets, list fetch/refresh strategy).
  internal/blocking/matcher adapts the design of blocky v0.35.0
  cache/stringcache: the length-bucketed sorted concatenated-string exact
  set searched by binary search, the cheapest-first matcher chain with
  per-list matched-rule reporting, and the regex-count warning threshold.
  internal/upstream takes the parallel_best strategy (race two randomly
  chosen healthy upstreams, first usable answer wins) and the strict
  strategy from blocky's resolver package, and internal/cache follows its
  caching resolver (prefetch of entries hit often within a window, packed
  messages as cache values, never caching conditional or local answers).
  No blocky source file is copied verbatim.
- dnsproxy (https://github.com/AdguardTeam/dnsproxy), Apache-2.0: linked as
  the upstream client library of internal/upstream (plain, TCP, DoT, DoH,
  DoQ, DoH3 and DNSCrypt transports, sdns:// stamps, bootstrap resolution;
  also the independent DoT/DoH/DoQ/DoH3 client in the internal/dnsserver
  tests); the dnsmasq-style "[/domain/]upstream" syntax accepted by
  upstream.ImportDnsmasq follows its upstream configuration format; the DoQ
  and DoH3 server structure in internal/dnsserver follows
  proxy/serverquic.go and proxy/serverhttps.go. Its dependencies
  AdguardTeam/golibs, AdguardTeam/dnscrypt and ameshkov/dnsstamps are
  public domain (Unlicense) and robfig/cron/v3 is MIT, Copyright (C) 2012
  Rob Figueiredo.
- CoreDNS (https://github.com/coredns/coredns), Apache-2.0: zone tree,
  secondary-transfer flow, test helpers; the DoQ and DoH3 listeners in
  internal/dnsserver follow core/dnsserver/server_quic.go and
  server_https3.go (stream worker pool, per-connection stream cap, RFC 9250
  error handling, HTTP/3 connection limit). internal/zone adapts the design
  of plugin/file/tree (a left-leaning red-black tree with one node per
  owner name holding every RRset of that name, names ordered label by
  label from the right; CoreDNS's tree is itself derived from the biogo
  LLRB, BSD-3-Clause) and the lookup order of plugin/file/lookup.go (zone
  cuts, exact match, CNAME chase, closest-encloser wildcard); the zone and
  authoritative-stage golden tests follow the plugin/test.Case style. No
  CoreDNS source file is copied verbatim.
- quic-go (https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go), MIT: QUIC and HTTP/3
  transport for the DoQ and DoH3 listeners.
- external-dns (https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/external-dns), Apache-2.0:
  Endpoint record shape and the webhook provider contract.
- Kubernetes apiextensions-apiserver (https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes,
  module k8s.io/apiextensions-apiserver), Apache-2.0: linked as a library for
  CRD schema, defaulting and CEL validation; the custom-resource admission
  sequence in internal/store/validator mirrors pkg/registry/customresource.
- go-oidc (https://github.com/coreos/go-oidc), Apache-2.0, with go-jose
  (https://github.com/go-jose/go-jose), Apache-2.0: OIDC discovery, JWKS
  and ID token verification; its oidctest helpers back the mock OpenID
  Provider in tests.
- golang.org/x/oauth2 and golang.org/x/crypto, BSD-3-Clause, Copyright The
  Go Authors: authorization code + PKCE client; bcrypt in tests only.
  golang.org/x/sync, BSD-3-Clause, Copyright The Go Authors: singleflight
  coalescing of identical cache misses in internal/cache.
  golang.org/x/net/publicsuffix, BSD-3-Clause, Copyright The Go Authors:
  the registrable domain (eTLD+1) recorded for query-log names in
  internal/querylog/sqlitelog, which also stores querylog.db on
  modernc.org/sqlite.
- Kubernetes (https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes), Apache-2.0: the
  shape of claimValidationRules and claimMappings follows the apiserver's
  structured authentication configuration.
- dex (https://github.com/dexidp/dex), Apache-2.0: the OIDC end-to-end test
  runs an unmodified dex release as a separate process; dex is not linked
  into or distributed with kudurru.

Test data (not compiled into the binary):

- StevenBlack/hosts (https://github.com/StevenBlack/hosts), MIT, Copyright
  (c) 2023 Steven Black: internal/blocking/testdata/corpus/stevenblack/hosts
  is data/StevenBlack/hosts at commit 2025dea10a1d, unmodified; licence and
  provenance are in the same directory.
- Kubernetes client libraries (https://github.com/kubernetes/client-go,
  k8s.io/api, k8s.io/apimachinery, k8s.io/apiextensions-apiserver),
  Apache-2.0: dependencies of the kube store driver (informers, server-side
  apply, coordination.k8s.io Lease leader election); internal/controller
  uses the client-go rate-limited workqueue and follows the client-go
  controller pattern (watch-fed cache, keyed queue, periodic resync), and
  internal/controller/kubeevents uses its core/v1 Event recorder.
- controller-runtime (https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/controller-runtime),
  Apache-2.0: client, informer cache and envtest used by the kube store
  driver and its tests; the Watch catch-up barrier is informed by its
  read-your-writes consistency client, and the envtest binary layout
  (bin/k8s/<version>-<os>-<arch>) follows its setup-envtest tool.
- modernc.org/sqlite (https://gitlab.com/cznic/sqlite), BSD-3-Clause: cgo-free
  SQLite used for local.db.

